  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 506,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 545,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70516,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 133,
        "headingId": 545,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours are asymptomatic intratesticular masses.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T11:56:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 507,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 546,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70517,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 133,
        "headingId": 546,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients are 29&ndash;69&nbsp;years of age {30549139; 28739499; 18835626}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T11:56:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 508,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 547,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70518,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 133,
        "headingId": 547,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T11:56:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 509,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 548,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70519,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 133,
        "headingId": 548,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours show mutations of the <em>CTNNB1</em> gene {28739499; 29705715}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T11:56:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 516,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 555,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70520,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 133,
        "headingId": 555,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The cut surface of the testis shows a small, well-circumscribed, solid, white to grey lesion, 10&ndash;28&nbsp;mm in diameter {30549139}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T11:56:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 510,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 549,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70521,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 133,
        "headingId": 549,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours are surrounded by a thick fibrous capsule and lobulated by thin fibrous septa. Tumour cells are arranged in solid nests and trabeculae in a background of loose oedematous stroma. Most parts of the tumour consist of PAS- and mucin-negative signet ring&ndash;like cells with eccentric nuclei and large cytoplasmic vacuoles and may contain eosinophilic cells or sclerotic areas {28739499}. The possibility that signet ring stromal tumour is a specific morphological pattern of Sertoli cell tumour with unique histopathological features was first suggested by Kuo et al. {18835626}, and this opinion has been recently supported by others {30110596; 32604170}. These authors compared the morphological and immunohistochemical features of pancreatic solid pseudopapillary neoplasms and testicular Sertoli cell tumours and found significant differences between them, demonstrating the value of the continued separate classification of testis tumours and pseudopapillary pancreatic neoplasms {32604170}.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>The tumours are positive for vimentin, nuclear &beta;-catenin, cyclin D1, S100, CD10, NSE, and synaptophysin. They are negative for inhibin, calretinin, actin, desmin, and melan-A {28739499}.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>The most important differential diagnosis is with metastatic signet-ring cell carcinoma because of its distinct prognosis and treatment. Signet ring stromal tumours do not secrete mucin, and immunoreactivity for vimentin and negativity for cytokeratin and EMAs help rule out metastases.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T11:56:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 511,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 550,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70522,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 133,
        "headingId": 550,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T11:56:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 512,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 551,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70523,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 133,
        "headingId": 551,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Mutations of the <em>CTNNB1</em> gene have been identified {28739499; 29705715}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T11:56:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 515,
    "bookid": 36,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 554,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 70524,
        "bookId": 36,
        "chapterId": 133,
        "headingId": 554,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a solid neoplasm with signet-ring cells.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> positive immunostaining for vimentin and negativity for cytokeratins; positivity for &beta;-catenin in selected cases.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2022-02-22T11:56:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 513,
